/**
 * @defgroup ScriptingAPI C# Scripting API
 * @brief C# API for game scripting in the Wiesel Engine.
 *
 * The scripting API provides C# classes and components for building
 * game logic. Scripts derive from MonoBehavior and are attached to
 * entities as components.
 *
 * @section scripting_lifecycle Script Lifecycle
 *
 * - MonoBehavior.OnStart() - called once when the entity enters the scene
 * - MonoBehavior.OnUpdate(float deltaTime) - called every frame
 * - MonoBehavior.OnFixedUpdate(float fixedDeltaTime) - called at fixed physics rate
 * - MonoBehavior.OnDestroy() - called when the entity is destroyed
 *
 * @section scripting_components Components
 *
 * Access components via GetComponent<T>() on MonoBehavior or Entity:
 *
 * - TransformComponent - position, rotation, scale
 * - ModelComponent - 3D model rendering
 * - CameraComponent - camera projection and FOV
 * - RigidBodyComponent - physics body
 * - BoxColliderComponent, SphereColliderComponent - collision shapes
 * - LightDirectComponent, LightPointComponent - lighting
 * - AudioSourceComponent - positional audio
 * - AnimatorComponent - skeletal animation
 * - SpriteRendererComponent, SpriteAnimatorComponent - 2D sprites
 * - TextComponent - text rendering
 * - UIDocumentComponent - RmlUi documents with data binding
 * - CanvasComponent - UI canvas layout
 *
 * @section scripting_statics Static APIs
 *
 * - Input - keyboard, mouse, gamepad queries
 * - Physics - raycasting and overlap queries
 * - Audio - fire-and-forget sound playback
 * - Settings - runtime graphics and audio options
 * - SceneManager - scene loading and transitions
 * - Console - developer console commands
 * - Time - delta time, total time, frame count
 * - Cursor - custom cursor states
 */